menu "PixeLED scripts"

    config PX_SCRIPTS
        bool "Glow scripts: animations written and run on the device"
        default y
        help
            Animations in the Glow language (docs/glow.md): written in the web UI, kept on
            LittleFS, compiled on the device and run by a small machine in the render task.
            Without it the firmware has none of it: no code, no RAM, no web page.

    config PX_SCRIPT_SLOTS
        int "Scripts at most"
        depends on PX_SCRIPTS
        range 1 16
        default 16
        help
            How many scripts the device keeps (their animation numbers 200 to 215). A script
            takes no RAM until it is shown: its record (152 bytes of /fs/scripts/index.bin), its
            source and its program are files, its style and sliders an NVS key of 18 bytes.

endmenu
